# Story 103: The Mobile App (50s)
# Hook: rysh in your pocket. Reach your panes from iOS or Android.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-103-the-mobile-app.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
rysh in your pocket. Reach your panes from iOS or Android.

[00:05.0 --> 00:14.0]
rysh-mobile is the native app for iOS and Android. You log in once, and your workspaces are right there on your phone.

[00:14.0 --> 00:25.0]
The flow is a simple drill-down: pick a workspace, see its list of panes, tap a pane to open the live pane view.

[00:25.0 --> 00:36.0]
Each pane renders with XTerm.js, so colors and ANSI look exactly like your desktop terminal.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
On shared panes you even get a fully interactive terminal -- run vim or htop from your phone and the keystrokes flow straight through.

[00:45.0 --> 00:50.0]
Your agentic terminal, anywhere you are.

